{"_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": ""}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "External Peripheral Types"}, {"type": "position", "content": 3}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 1}, {"type": "level", "content": "B1.2"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you hear and use to talk about external peripheral types."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Build the user interface, supported on the prototype assessment, determining the inputs and outputs required in the design and defining the navigation guidelines, according to the user's needs. Identifies different hardware components and peripheral devices."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Discusses a range of options for potential actions at work through the correct use of grammar, vocabulary; level of formality and purpose, and cohesion and coherence aspects appropriate to this level.  Exchanges simple information on the hardware devices and the architecture of a system to create the IT solution."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "enpe8n6le01ob03re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Where to + Verb"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use <span class=\"strong\">where to + verb</span> to give emphasis to a place in a sentence."}, {"type": "example", "content": "I need to know where to buy some devices to complement the gift. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "If you get a new device, you must know where to plug it in. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "He'd love a subwoofer, I can tell you where to get it. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "I don't know where to begin with the list! "}, {"type": "text", "content": "  <span class=\"strong\"> Where</span> refers to a location or a place. It helps us provide a context to a sentence depending on the action. When we include a verb in infinitive after the word <b>where</b>, we can omit the subject of the sentence in order not to repeat it. <br /> <br />Let's review these sentences:<br /><span class=\"italic\">I need to know where I can go to buy some external peripherals. </span><br /><span class=\"italic\">I need to know <span class=\"strong\"> where to go</span> in order to buy some external peripherals. </span></span><br /><br />  In the previous sentence we can see how the emphasis goes in<span class=\"strong\"> the place</span>."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "External Peripheral Types"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use different types of connections to add <span class=\"strong\"> external peripheral devices</span> to a computer."}, {"type": "example", "content": "It has many USB ports, they're common because you can connect and disconnect devices easily without rebooting the unit. "}, {"type": "example", "content": " It's also FireWire compatible; in other words, you can get high definition audio and video. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Non-removable storage include external or network hard drives. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "When we talk about external peripheral devices, we refer to all of those devices that can be connected in the slots that a CPU has on its surface. There are different types of external peripherals that help us achieve various tasks. <br /><br />You can identify the different types of external peripherals in the next chart:"}, {"type": "image", "content": "enpe8n6le01ob03img01.jpg"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "install"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to include a new part into something"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: There's no need to open the case and install new parts as most computers are designed with slots to plug in these types of devices. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n6le01ob03aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "driver "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a program that allows the computer to recognize devices"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The device must come with a driver so the computer recognizes it. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n6le01ob03aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "firewire"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a high definition audio or video connection"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: It's also FireWire compatible; in other words, you can get high definition audio and video."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n6le01ob03aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "subwoofer"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "speakers with quality sound options "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: He'd love a subwoofer. I can tell you where to get it."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n6le01ob03aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "removable "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "when something can be taken apart "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Removable storage covers any type of storage connected externally like flash drives or DVD's. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n6le01ob03aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "non-removable "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "when something is fixed to another object"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Non-removable storage include external or network hard drives. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n6le01ob03aud06"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Look for information about external peripheral devices."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Choose 2 connections and 3 devices"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Draw those connections and devices and next to the pictures write a description about each one of them."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Make a brochure to promote these connections and devices with your pictures and their description."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Share your brochure to your partners. "}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I search information about external peripheral devices."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I describe each type of connection and devices as part of peripheral external devices."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I share with some partners"}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}], "type": "sena", "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"template_override": 1, "_data": [], "type": "welcome", "id": 0, "contents": [{}]}, {"template_override": 1, "contents": [{"value": {"images": [{"time": "0", "image": "enpe8n6le01ob03re2img01.jpg", "id": 0, "text": "<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Robert</strong>: The computer you bought for our son is amazing! I need to know where to buy some devices to complement the gift.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Jackeline</strong>: We aren't supposed to open the CPU's case; we could lose the warranty. You must get him external peripherals devices.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Robert</strong>: What are those?</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Jackeline</strong>: External peripheral devices are externally connected to the computer. There's no need to open the case and install new parts as most computers are designed with slots to plug in these types of devices. Thus, make sure you know the type of device that you want and the type of connection that it needs.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Robert</strong>: How would I know that?</p>"}, {"time": "34500", "image": "enpe8n6le01ob03re2img02.jpg", "id": 1, "text": "<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Jackeline</strong>: Look at the slots in the CPU; they define the types of connections available. If you get a new device, you must know where to plug it in. Actually, there are many types of devices you can buy for him. He'd love a subwoofer. I can tell you where to get it.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Robert</strong>: Ok, but tell me more about the type of connection this computer has.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Jackeline</strong>: It has many USB ports. They're common because you can connect and disconnect devices easily without rebooting the unit. It's also FireWire compatible; in other words, you can get high definition audio and video. Finally, it has a PS/2 connection, but don't worry about it since it's only for the mouse and keyboard.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Robert</strong>: Cool, and what type of devices are there?</p>"}, {"time": "75500", "image": "enpe8n6le01ob03re2img03.jpg", "id": 2, "text": "<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Jackeline</strong>: I don't know where to begin with the list! Removable storage covers any type of storage connected externally like flash drives or DVDs. Non-removable storage includes external or network hard drives. Besides, there are input devices like scanners or microphones and output devices like cameras or monitors. The device must come with a driver so the computer recognizes it.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Robert</strong>: I'll get him that subwoofer, then.</p>"}], "coverimg": "enpe8n6le01ob03re2img01.jpg", "audiosrc": "enpe8n6le01ob03re2aud01"}, "type": "slideshow"}], "type": "audio", "_data": [], "id": 1, "title": ""}], "exercises": [{"stimuli_ids": [0], "template_override": 1, "questions": [], "type": "WLC", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can talk about external periphe